changes={
('.data','data_flow'):'The block-requirement query and save-submission routine write compressed length plus0x38 and the active snapshot pointer into the first descriptor entry. Load installs the destination pointer but does not recompute file_size. Preparation itself writes the snapshot record, banner and description, not the descriptor.',
('.data','inferred_type'):'Initialized writable data begins with a0x2C-byte descriptor:20 icon-metadata bytes and two12-byte CardEntry records, terminated by file_size=-1. Existing source/split objects contain228/232 bytes including diagnostics, localized labels, timestamp format and archive/resource strings; the four-byte difference is trailing padding. Objects were inspected without rebuilding.',
('8001D2BC','inferred_type'):'void lbSnap_8001D2BC(void). Polls two card_state elements and the first two elements of the three-element state_changed array. Communicates through the singleton, without using the third change slot.',
('8001D40C','data_flow'):'Clears the selected change flag and passes the127-entry catalog and capacity outputs to lb_8001BFD8. The lower layer filters current-disc company/game identifiers and filenames whose first character is a digit, parses their numeric prefix with strtoul, sorts descending timestamps and writes file_no=-1 sentinels. This is not validation that the entire filename is decimal. On success the wrapper counts through the first sentinel, capped at127.',
('8001DC0C','data_flow'):'Receives the capture buffer supplied by Camera Mode, writes type4,640x480, stage and item/fighter metadata, encoder mode3 and compressed result into the snapshot work record. It invokes banner generation to place64x32 sampled pixels inside a96x32 banner, then writes a localized description with month/day/time. The Camera Mode caller next calculates required card blocks.',
('8001DC0C','purpose'):'Prepares the captured image for snapshot storage: initializes metadata, encodes the640x480 image with a256000-byte capacity, generates a64x32 image inside the96x32 Memory Card banner, and formats a localized timestamp description.',
('8001DC0C','state_behavior'):'Writes the snapshot fields and calls the encoder. Nonzero encoder result yields1, zero yields0. Banner generation and description formatting run in either case; failure does not roll back metadata or other writes. Camera Mode advances to state2 after1 and returns to state0 after0.',
('8001DE8C','purpose'):'For type4 snapshots, attempts JPEG decoding into the supplied destination, then flushes snapshot-metadata width*height*2 bytes regardless of decoder success. The flush range is not derived from JPEG dimensions and does not establish that all decoded pixels are covered.',
('8001DE8C','inferred_type'):'int lbSnap_8001DE8C(void* dst), returning1 for nonzero decoder result and0 otherwise. For normal640x480 images the tiled RGB565 output occupies614400 bytes. Decoder writes follow dimensions parsed from JPEG and use16-pixel block rounding, while this wrapper flushes dimensions from snapshot metadata; it does not check their agreement or destination capacity.',
('8001DE8C','state_behavior'):'Non-type4 returns0 without decode or cache flush. Type4 invokes the decoder and then flushes snapshot width*height*2 bytes even on decoder failure. JPEG dimensions determine decoder traversal and are not compared to snapshot dimensions. The decoder has nonlocal error returns, but this wrapper supplies no independent bounds or format validation.',
('8001E218','state_behavior'):'Unconditionally installs both pointers, sets only card_result for slots0/1 to8, and loads the icon resource. It does not initialize catalog counts, entries, capacities, description, probe states or change flags and has no local null/duplicate-setup guard. Separate lifecycle routines clear work pointers or reset icon/probe state.',
('8001E27C','inferred_type'):'void lbSnap_8001E27C(void), a returning routine with no return value. It writes NULL to the snapshot-work and slot-array pointers; it neither frees those caller-owned allocations nor resets the rest of the singleton.',
('8001D4A4','state_behavior'):'Increment the unsigned-second candidate on a cached timestamp collision and restart scanning until no match remains. Uniqueness is relative to the supplied cached catalog, not a fresh card scan. Only the output buffer is explicitly written; preserving catalog state requires that output not alias it.',
('8001D3E8','game_mapping'):'Supplies the selected snapshot block count to the album copy-capacity guard; the caller, not this accessor, compares it with destination free blocks and decides whether to proceed.'}
